  "caption": "Quinn's knees had opinions about stairs, the internet said to lose weight before moving, and Quinn started to feel guilty. It isn't a matter of fault.\n\nExercise can ease knee arthritis pain and help function even without any change in weight. When weight does change, the benefits can add up, especially alongside exercise.\n\nWhat can help: start with movement you enjoy, choose low-impact options like water exercise, cycling or seated strength if walking hurts, build strength to support the knee, bring in a dietitian for nutrition and your GP for medical advice, and remember even modest changes can be worthwhile.\n\nGet it checked if the knee is hot, very swollen, giving way, or pain keeps building.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
